# Continents to rebuild, cheapest first (mbtiles+pbf), one per line.
# The runner re-reads this file before each region, so it can be edited
# freely while the chain is running — never edit the runner itself.
# Comment a line out to skip it.
#
# 2026-09-18 (post viewer merge b861cc4): trimmed to the regions that need an
# actual BUILD. Everything else from this round failed at gate or upload, not
# at build, so their ZIMs exist and only need a viewer swap + re-gate — hours
# of rebuild would buy nothing. Builds from here bake the merged viewer
# automatically (create_osm_zim reads resources/viewer at assembly).
#
# australia-nz : 2026-09-14 gate-failed on two zero-byte satellite cache tiles
#                (14/13426/9043-9044); caches cleared, create_osm_zim now drops
#                empty raster files.
# africa       : 2026-09-15 overture-failed on a duckdb HTTP timeout fetching
#                addresses part-00024. Transient; retry.
# russia       : never shipped this round (newest local is 2026-05-12c).
# canada       : never shipped.
australia-nz
africa
russia
canada

# 2026-09-19: new regions requested to give developing-world users a
# reasonably sized download instead of the 23 GB whole-continent africa.
# Registry rows added the same day (cloud/regions.tsv).
#   north-africa   : Maghreb - only egypt covered the north before this.
#   central-africa : DRC/Congo/Gabon/Cameroon - fell between west- and
#                    southern-africa's boxes, uncovered.
#   horn-of-africa : Ethiopia/Somalia/Eritrea - overlaps east-africa but
#                    ships a smaller, sharper download.
#   east-polynesia : pacific-islands stops at 180 deg, so Samoa/Tonga/
#                    Cook Is./French Polynesia were uncovered.
north-africa
central-africa
horn-of-africa
east-polynesia

# The four above are commented out until their PBF/mbtiles/search extracts
# exist under world-data/regions/. Uncomment once extraction finishes --
# build-region-fast.sh takes those paths as given and would fail instantly.
